{%- comment -%}
  Google click-id capture.

  Included from layout/theme.liquid, immediately before </body>.

  Shopify caps order.landing_site at 255 characters and Google Shopping puts gclid LAST
  in the query string, so server-side the gclid always arrives as a 4-character stump
  ("CjwK") while gbraid survives. A stump is worse than nothing — Google accepts it and
  attributes it to no click. Cart attributes have no such cap and become order
  note_attributes, which is the only route by which a complete gclid can reach
  agents/ads-conversion-uploader.

  Loaded `defer` and off the critical path: this exists to measure paid traffic and must
  not cost the page speed that traffic is paying for. On any page that is not an ad
  landing it does nothing and issues no request.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'rsc-click-id.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
